<Concept title="States">
  <p>Behavioral definitions for the game's runtime states — the rules behind how the player moves between the city, free-explore fields, and authored quests, plus the systems that ride on top.</p>

  <p>These pages are normative. The key words <strong>MUST</strong>, <strong>MUST NOT</strong>, <strong>REQUIRED</strong>, <strong>SHALL</strong>, <strong>SHOULD</strong>, <strong>MAY</strong>, and <strong>OPTIONAL</strong> are used as described in RFC 2119 — they define expected behavior, not current implementation status.</p>

  <h2>Definitions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/states/quest-vs-field">Quest vs Field</a> — the City / Field / Quest macro-states and how <code>SessionManager</code> transitions between them.</li>
    <li><a href="/states/telepipe">Telepipe</a> — the single-slot telepipe lifecycle, the one-active rule, and round-trip return behavior.</li>
    <li><a href="/states/story-progression">Story Progression</a> — completed-mission flags, quest prerequisite gates, and how the guild counter derives REPORT / LOCKED / CLEAR.</li>
    <li><a href="/states/quest-objectives">Quest Objectives</a> — objective schema, count tracking, and how completion gates the report action.</li>
    <li><a href="/states/enemies">Enemies</a> — the roster, the behavior state machine, status effects, and per-model SFX.</li>
  </ul>
</Concept>
